From bd31186d10dddaca86f64a9347725e31e23486dd Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Nakata Maho <maho.nakata@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 30 Sep 2026 13:44:32 +0900
Subject: [PATCH] Execute undefined opcodes as a Zilog Z80 with
 Z80_NO_EXCEPTION

The ED, DD and FD tables leave undefined opcodes empty (196 ED entries,
90 DD and 90 FD entries). Without Z80_NO_EXCEPTION, OP_ED/OP_IX/OP_IY
throw "detect an unknown operand". With Z80_NO_EXCEPTION the check is
compiled out and the empty entry is called, so any such opcode (for
example ED 00, the NEG duplicate ED 4C, ED A4, or DD 00) crashes the
host with a null function call.

With Z80_NO_EXCEPTION, execute them as a Zilog Z80 does instead:

- undefined ED opcodes are two-byte NOPs (8 clocks);
- ED 4C/54/5C/64/6C/74/7C are NEG, ED 55/5D/65/6D/75/7D are RETN,
  ED 4E/66/6E are IM 0, ED 76 is IM 1 and ED 7E is IM 2;
- DD or FD before an opcode without an index form is ignored and the
  opcode runs unprefixed; this also covers repeated prefixes and DD ED.

The default configuration still throws, so test-unknown is unchanged.
test-undefined-opcodes checks all 256 opcodes of each table with
Z80_NO_EXCEPTION.
---
 test/Makefile                   |   5 ++
 test/test-undefined-opcodes.cpp | 141 ++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++
 z80.hpp                         |  72 ++++++++++++++--
 3 files changed, 212 insertions(+), 6 deletions(-)
 create mode 100644 test/test-undefined-opcodes.cpp

diff --git a/test/Makefile b/test/Makefile
index 8591d62..bc4f39b 100644
--- a/test/Makefile
+++ b/test/Makefile
@@ -25,6 +25,7 @@ all:
